# Docs, design, tests, safety

- Keep `CHANGELOG.md` in the project root. After every commit, add a date plus a short description of what changed for the user or developer. Group entries by version or date.
- Record important decisions and limits in an English code comment or a short `DECISIONS.md`.
- Update the README when how to run the project or its main features change.
- Early UI stays simple: standard platform components, clear behavior first. No complex animation or visual polish until a later, separate stage.
- Do not write tests for everything. Test critical paths only: keys, calculations, network calls, and security.
- Review the diff before committing.
- Never commit secrets, keys, seed phrases, or configs that contain passwords. Sensitive data goes in environment variables or secure storage.
